This is a question that must come up in this group about once a week, and 
all over the net daily!

There is still no answer to the problem though as there are two opposites 
who are both right.


As an ISP here we do not censor any news articles or groups from our 
feed.  Indeed some of those alt.* groups are very popular due to nice 
software the decodes pictures easily.

We dont have the problems with Janet.  They network is for educational 
purposes and as such it is fair to exclude these groups.  Janet is one of 
the authorities who may have some right to ban what goes over their lines 
as they are responsible for their own lines.

As for a Sysadmin stopping stuff, then thats also his right to do so due 
to inherited power.  Though it must be said that it is down to his 
employers as to what powers he should have over this flow.  In a uni all 
of the students are (theoretically :) ) old enough to decide for 
themselves what they want to see and what they deem tasteless.

Our policy here is one of hands off.  We have a signed agreement with all 
customers stating that they are responisble for hunting down these 
things, and they will only get them if they pull them off of our newserver.

I agree with you on the point that if they exclude groups then they lay 
open to people then assuming they are responisble for what goes on.  
There are so many groups it is likely that things in som of the comp.* 
groups may not be to their approval either, especially the advocacy 
groups, and even in the past uk.net!

